{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1417541140,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIwMTM3MDI5OQ=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1417541140,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIwMTM3MDMwMA=="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1417541140,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIwMTM3MDMwMQ=="},"added":["annex"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1425046980,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc2NDAxMzc0","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/26#issuecomment-76401374"},"message":"I just \"discovered\" this use case myself. However, in my case a simple \"not referenced after commit X\" is not enough. I have a large chunk of data that got annex'ed after some defined state of a data set that I need to preserve in history, but in the meantime it became obsolete and got replaced. I think what we might want is some kind of history squashing between commits X and Y.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1458649577,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE5OTc4Njg1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-199786852"},"message":"It sounds like this is obsolete now. @yarikoptic  please confirm and close if true.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1458650224,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE5OTc4OTUwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-199789508"},"message":"I think it still remains...  \n\n```\nIn [1]: from datalad.support.annexrepo import AnnexRepo\n\nIn [2]: AnnexRepo('/tmp/123123', create=True)\nOut[2]: \u003cAnnexRepo path=/tmp/123123 (\u003cclass 'datalad.support.annexrepo.AnnexRepo'\u003e)\u003e\n\nIn [3]: \n[1]  + 12283 suspended  ipython\n2 13310 -\u003e148 [1].....................................:Tue 22 Mar 2016 01:36:12 PM CET:.\nhopa:~datalad/datalad\n$\u003e cd /tmp/123123\nW: git-annex repositories not (yet) supported in the prompt\n2 13311 [1].....................................:Tue 22 Mar 2016 01:36:15 PM CET:.\nhopa:/tmp/123123\n$\u003e git annex info\nrepository mode: indirect\ntrusted repositories: 0\nsemitrusted repositories: 3\n    00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\n    00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002 -- bittorrent\n    5d2773e2-6ebb-4c99-9ba4-77d320ec0667 -- yoh@hopa:/tmp/123123 [here]\n...\n```\n\nbut the point either we should come up with anything better or just leave it alone...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1458650452,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE5OTc5MjM0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-199792348"},"message":"@yarikoptic Ah I misinterpreted the scope of \"identifier\". Indeed an open question.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1458655454,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE5OTgyOTU4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-199829580"},"message":"I guess, the only thing obvious would be to use the \"name\" of a dataset,\nusing the full submodule name from toplevel (or just basename('.') if there\nis no upper level. For example \"openfmri/ds0001\". But I'm not sure, whether\nthis is a good idea. If you have multiple installtions, it's still not an\n\"identifier\". But this is true for anything we could possibly come up with,\nas long as there is no central registry or sth. like this. So, the path at\nleast is not ambigous.\n\n2016-03-22 13:40 GMT+01:00 Michael Hanke notifications@github.com:\n\n\u003e @yarikoptic https://github.com/yarikoptic Ah I misinterpreted the scope\n\u003e of \"identifier\". Indeed an open question.\n\u003e \n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-199792348","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1458745420,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIwMDM4NDQ0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-200384447"},"message":"well -- to some degree original/default descriptions are the best since they uniquely identify any given clone / remote where annexed content resides.  But I don't think we should expose indeed internal paths which might change or pretty much might be \"irrelevant\" while sharing those datasets publicly.  E.g. in Michael's I see a wide range of representative examples:\n\n```\n$\u003e git annex info   \nrepository mode: indirect\ntrusted repositories: 0\nsemitrusted repositories: 8\n    00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 -- web\n    00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002 -- bittorrent\n    597f3147-141e-4c00-92db-5575aa69498e -- original source repository\n    664fbb24-ba44-44e4-95ec-e455333e987f -- mih@medusa:/home/data/psyinf/forrest_gump/incoming\n    731b805f-054e-485f-b3fc-79b460aa2482 -- Data graveyard\n    cb9b9552-c3d8-4aaf-84ed-532381978235 -- yoh@hopa:~/proj/datalad/providers/forrest_gump [here]\n    dd3d4b44-44f2-40d6-9d9e-30fd3ded5c26 -- original public releases (http://studyforrest.org) [origin]\n    f15331bb-20fd-4d40-93d0-6b8445f89d2c -- mih@meiner:~/forrest/anondata\n```\n\nsome are the \"private\" clones with default `user@host:path`, where some were provided manually.  I like \"original public releases (URL)\" since it identifies where is that and provides some reference url.  I don't like \"Data graveyard\" since it provides no contact reference.  So  may be we should adhere to smth like below given that this dataset's name was studyforrest/phase1\n- `datalad.org:studyforrest/phase1 (crawler)`\n- `datalad.org:studyforrest/phase1 (public)`\n- `datalad.org:studyforrest/phase1 (graveyard)`\n- ... with default paths from annex ...\n\n?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1471265641,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzOTc5NDY0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/27#issuecomment-239794642"},"message":"This is so old that is was re-envisioned: #701 Moreover #682 provides `get_dataset_identifier()` in the metadata context.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1471265641,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NzU1NjA5NzI2"},"status":2}]}